# --------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Two things this project has to commit, unlike a normal Astro site.
#
# public/frames/ — the encoded webp sequence. A deploy builds from a fresh
# clone, so if the frames are not in git there is nothing for the page to
# draw. They are generated output, which makes ignoring them the instinct.
# Do not. Re-running `scrollytelling frames` replaces the whole directory,
# so squash the history before publishing if it gets heavy.
#
# .scrollytelling-version — records what the template looked like when this
# project was generated. `scrollytelling scaffold . --diff` needs it to say
# what has moved since. Losing it costs you that report.
#
# Both are named below so a later broad rule cannot quietly sweep them up.
!public/frames/
!.scrollytelling-version
